meta {
  name: Generate Upload URL
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/articles/upload-url
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
      "articleFileName": "articles/2024/01/my-article.md",
      "contentType": "text/markdown"
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
}

docs {
  # Generate Pre-signed Upload URL
  
  Generates a pre-signed POST URL for uploading markdown articles directly to S3. The URL is valid for 5 minutes and includes validation constraints for file size and content type.
  
  ## Request Body
  
  - `s3Key` (string, required): The desired S3 key/path for the file to be uploaded
  - `s3Bucket` (string, optional): The S3 bucket name. If not provided, uses the `S3_ARTICLES_BUCKET_NAME` environment variable.
  - `contentType` (string, optional): The content type for the upload. Valid values:
    - `text/markdown` (default)
    - `text/plain`
  - `fileSize` (number, optional): Maximum file size in bytes. Defaults to 5MB (5242880 bytes).
  
  ## Response
  
  Success (200):
  ```json
  {
    "url": "https://meridiano-articles.s3.amazonaws.com",
    "fields": {
      "key": "articles/2024/01/my-article.md",
      "Content-Type": "text/markdown",
      "X-Amz-Algorithm": "AWS4-HMAC-SHA256",
      "X-Amz-Credential": "...",
      "X-Amz-Date": "...",
      "Policy": "...",
      "X-Amz-Signature": "..."
    },
    "expiresIn": 300
  }
  ```
  
  Error (400):
  ```json
  {
    "statusCode": 400,
    "message": "S3 bucket name not provided and S3_ARTICLES_BUCKET_NAME environment variable is not set"
  }
  ```
  
  ## How to Use the Response
  
  1. Create a FormData object with the returned `fields`
  2. Append your file to the FormData
  3. POST the FormData to the returned `url`
  
  Example (JavaScript):
  ```javascript
  const { url, fields } = response;
  const formData = new FormData();
  
  // Add all the fields first
  Object.entries(fields).forEach(([key, value]) => {
    formData.append(key, value);
  });
  
  // Add the file last
  formData.append('file', fileBlob);
  
  // Upload to S3
  await fetch(url, {
    method: 'POST',
    body: formData
  });
  ```
  
  ## Security & Constraints
  
  - Pre-signed URL expires after 5 minutes (300 seconds)
  - File size limited to 5MB by default (customizable via `fileSize` parameter)
  - Content type restricted to `text/markdown` or `text/plain`
  - S3 enforces these constraints server-side during upload
  
  ## Next Steps
  
  After successfully uploading to S3, call the `POST /api/articles/markdown` endpoint with the same `s3Key` to process the uploaded file.
}
